title: subscribee-as-such must be a metadata property.
pid: 08ec328a-e9ba-4650-81f5-9ff6d716e1c9
body: |2-
  The metadata should in effect say
  "this is node <ID> as a subscribee presented by subscriber <ID>".

  Otherwise the user could copy the subscribee
  to somewhere outside of the collection of subscribees.
  If it is owned, that could destroy a lot of its content relationships,
  because they were being hidden from the subscribee-as-such view.

  This requires no additional signaling to the user --
  a subscribee-as-such is already visually obvious to the user.
